  "discussion": "A moderate, medium period north swell will gradually decline over he next couple of days. The bulk of the swell was aimed just east of the state, but surf along north-facing shores of Big Island and Maui will remain elevated at the High Surf Advisory level through much of the night. North shore surf and the magnitude of the harbor surges will slowly decline on Tuesday and fade on Wednesday. Small background northwest and north swells will keep small to tiny surf in place Wednesday through Friday, then a small north-northwest swell will be possible during the weekend. Rough surf along east-facing shores will remain above seasonal average through Tuesday due to elevated trade wind swell and some wrapping north swell. East shore surf is expected to be around seasonal average Wednesday and Thursday, followed by a brief and slight increase Friday and Saturday. Mainly small background level surf will persist along south-facing shores during the next several days, with a small long-period swell possible on Friday.",
